  "recommendation": "false positive",
  "rationale": "The modeled password source is a generic credential-store accessor. The hashed material is a scoped 32-byte cryptographically random authority key used to derive a domain-separated continuity identifier. Production enrollment and missing-key recovery create it with secrets.token_bytes(32); persisted and migrated material is base64-decoded and required to be exactly 32 bytes. No production caller supplies a human password. The identifier is included in separately authenticated marker, snapshot, and rollback-floor contracts, not used as a standalone password verifier. The pinned rule help recommends SHA-2 or SHA-3 for high-entropy data outside the limited-input-space password case.",
  "production_hash_calls": [
